From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:58:06 +0900
Subject: startplasmamobile: let Qt pick the platform theme,
 as Plasma's desktop session does

startplasmamobile exported QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME=KDE, a leftover of the 2019 kwinwrapper that set up
the whole session by hand. It now ends in startplasma-wayland, which sets XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=KDE,
KDE_FULL_SESSION=true and KDE_SESSION_VERSION=6 as on the desktop; Qt picks the KDE platform theme
from those (the plugin's key is "kde").

Forced through the environment, the theme also reached the temporary QGuiApplication some
programs make before their real one, which asks for no desktop settings (Krita's OpenGL probe,
setDesktopSettingsAware(false) in a KDE session). The KDE theme connected the session bus there,
and Qt resumes a default bus's suspended delivery with a call queued to that application: gone
with it, the program's session bus stayed deaf for its whole life. With
PLASMA_INTEGRATION_USE_PORTAL=1 every portal file dialog then waited forever for its Response and
its invisible modal shell blocked the program (docs/103).

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-01
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [the line is redundant upstream too]
X-Rungic-Tests: none (gap: checked by hand with Krita, docs/103)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/103
